r\nfreezes the UI). Add ",[142,155,156],{},".await",": ",[142,159,160],{},"commands::open(app, serial, …).await?",".\nMSRV is now 1.90.",[134,163,164,167,168,171,172,175,176,179,180,183,184,187,188,191,192,195],{},[137,165,166],{},"JS package:"," ",[142,169,170],{},"exports"," now has separate ",[142,173,174],{},"import","\u002F",[142,177,178],{},"require"," entries with their own\ntypes (",[142,181,182],{},"index.d.cts","); the ",[142,185,186],{},"development"," condition pointing at ",[142,189,190],{},"guest-js\u002F*.ts"," and\nthe ",[142,193,194],{},"guest-js"," sources in the npm tarball are gone.",[134,197,198,203,204,207,208,210],{},[137,199,200],{},[142,201,202],{},"read()"," now reads bytes and decodes them in JS with the port's ",[142,205,206],{},"encoding"," and a\nstreaming decoder (UTF-8 characters split across reads are kept). It no longer calls\nthe native ",[142,209,152],{}," command.",[134,212,213,218,219,222,223,225,226,229,230,233],{},[137,214,215],{},[142,216,217],{},"watch()"," no longer uses the port's read ",[142,220,221],{},"timeout"," (1 s by default) as its batch\nwindow. Without ",[142,224,221],{}," \u002F ",[142,227,228],{},"serialDataFlushIntervalMs"," data is delivered within\n~20 ms and as soon as ",[142,231,232],{},"size"," bytes are buffered.",[134,235,236,239,240,243],{},[137,237,238],{},"CMUX"," is now real 3GPP 27.010 basic mode (0xF9 framing, SABM\u002FUA, CLD); before,\nthe frames were not understood by modems. ",[142,241,242],{},"openMuxChannel(dlci)"," accepts 1–63.",[134,245,246,249,250,254,255,258],{},[137,247,248],{},"Android:"," the plugin no longer offers the app for ",[251,252,253],"em",{},"every"," USB device (the old\n",[142,256,257],{},"device_filter.xml"," had a catch-all entry); it matches the supported chips plus any\nCDC-ACM device.",[134,260,261,267,268,271,272,275,276,279],{},[137,262,263,264],{},"Rust ",[142,265,266],{},"commands::open"," takes two more optional arguments at the end: ",[142,269,270],{},"dtr",",